he `erlhooks` post-pass (`require('cartograph.erlhooks').attach(data)` → `data.erlhooks`: `.unregistered`, `.unrun`, `.verbs`): hedged `ref` edges tagged `hook = key` from every dispatch site to the handlers registered under its key; registrations from the derived interpreter's tuples and direct calls, dispatch verbs = calls into the registry module that INVOKE (dynamic call / apply). ejabberd: 530 registrations, 257 dispatch sites, 750 edges, 55 hooks run with no registration, 372 handlers reachable only through a hook |\n| Which handle_call/handle_cast clause does a gen_server message reach — and which gen_statem clause (handle_event/4, or the state functions)? Which specific clauses does nothing in the tree send to? | the `erlmsg` post-pass (`require('cartograph.erlmsg').attach(data)` → `data.erlmsg`: `.rows`, `.unreached`; `erlmsg.unify(p, ps, v, vs)` three-valued): hedged `ref` edges tagged `msg = call|cast`, `clauses = {lines}`; the server explicit (?MODULE, a module atom, or built from one through a binding / single-clause helper / same-file macro) or chosen by the message among SPECIFIC clauses. gen_statem by callback mode (handle_event_function: handle_event/4 with the event type admitted; state_functions: every state function, gen_statem's own arity-3 callbacks excluded from the otp-api profile). ejabberd: 120 sites (24 gen_statem), 118 reach a clause, 92 edges, 16 specific clauses unreached |\n| Which definition does a same-file call reach when the preprocessor picks one per build? | the `erlvariants` post-pass (`require('cartograph.erlvariants').attach(data)`): a `samefile` refusal whose candidates sit in mutually exclusive -ifdef/-ifndef/-else branches becomes rule `variants` (+ `macro`) with a hedged `variant` edge to each definition |\n| Run the enrichment passes the open path runs (xlang, sql, frameworks, k8s/proto, erlreg, db) over extracted data | `require('cartograph.postpass').run(data, { say = fn, skip = { name = true } })` — `PASSES` is the one