cartograph.tblshape` — ARRAY `$arr` / RECORD `$rec` / MAP `$map`, accesses polymorphic `$idx`/`$set`; a Lua local gets a fresh JS name whenever the name is visible). Three layers: EMIT refusals by name (a general goto, a non-continue label, a multi-valued last entry of a Map constructor), PARSE by node's own parser (`node --check`, must be 0), RUN each module loaded under node, by outcome (ok / LuaBreak = a pack gap reached, named / LuaError / JS error). MEASURED 2026-09-29 over lua/ (321 files, 36 s): 26 refusals in 9 files, 0 parse failures; modules that LOAD: 254 → 266 (metatables: a WeakMap by identity, 5.1 semantics) → 267 (HOST pack: io files as userdata, os dates/env/exit/remove/rename/execute, `debug.getinfo(1, \"S\")` mapped back to the Lua source via LUAJS_SRC_ROOT); → 273 (Lua patterns: LuaJIT's matcher transliterated from C by tools/cjs.lua) → 314 of 326 (the VIM host pack: nvim's OWN pure-Lua runtime — vim/_core/shared, inspect, uri, fs, the module set DERIVED from the pack's requires — transliterated beside the modules and loaded lazily as nvim defers it; vim.uv / fn / json / mpack / system / env / NIL / log / notify as declared templates matched to probed nvim behaviour; the editor surfaces abort by name at the read; a shape is an optimization — a key the shape cannot hold goes to a hidden SIDE Map, never an abort; pcall never swallows a LuaBreak). The rest, every one a named break: loadstring 7 (Lua source built at run time), the editor 4, a script without its job file 1. The SEMANTICS oracle is `tests/luajs_spec.lua` (differential: Lua with the standard print vs the emitted JS under node, byte-identical). CART-1197 |\n| Declare HOW a Lua construct becomes JS as a PAIR OF EXAMPLES (not code) — the local half of the transliterator | `lua/cartograph/luajs/rules.lua` `M.RULES`: `{ lua = 'a + b', js = '$add(a, b)' }` — both sides READ by the lossless reader (`cartograph.algebraread`, the JS side as javascript), every Lua identifier a hole, the left MATCHED on a node's term modulo layout (gaps and comments dropped), the right INSTANTIATED and printed (algebra match / instantiate / cst_print); hole modes `as = { f = 'name' \\| 'raw' \\| 'block' }`; compile refuses a rule that drops a hole. 31 rules (literals, grouping, indexing, the operators, do, return 0/1); the CONTEXT cases (scope, calls, tables, loops, if, goto, number/string values) stay in `cartograph.luajs`. `algebraread.read_tree(src, lang, tree, visit)` gives each node of a caller's tree its term. `tools/luajs.lua` reports `RULES: n declared, m match(es); k never fired` (a rule no source reaches has no witness). Acceptance of the move: all 357 emitted files BYTE-IDENTICAL to the hand emitter; luajs_spec pins every rule firing — which then surfaced CART-1200 (no values returned ONE nil), fixed as a deliberate output change (`return $mv();`, normalized diff otherwise empty). CART-1199 |\n| Check the Lua→JS transliteration on EVERY program up to a size (not a sample) — control flow, value counts, coercions | `nvim --headless -u NONE -l tools/luajsgen.lua <control\\|values\\|coercion> <max size> [corpus dir] [out dir] [min=<n>]` — `cartograph.luajs.gencheck`: every program of the fragment runs under real Lua (luaref) and, transliterated, under node, compared per program. Prints the COUNT per size first, then the FUNNEL (generated → parses → loads → terminates → emitted → compared → diverged, + Lua-rejected programs the emitter translated anyway), a census of the compared programs by token, UNREACHED tokens (the claim is vacuous for them), divergences by class (value · message · crash · hang, smallest first; a failed node batch is bisected to its program), and the CLAIM with its four parameters (\"exhaustive to size N over the productions of CORPUS ∩ fragment F, atoms P\" — never promoted to proven by raising N). MEASURED 2026-09-29 at size 8 over lua/ (every divergence in <out>/diverged.txt): control 114,838 compared / 0 diverged (goto in 758, for in 512; atoms