ournal entries (and which DECISIONS) wrote this commit? Does the provenance travel with the repo? (the ledger) | Every journal entry records `decided_by` (`tactic` / `direct`) and `decisions = { { kind, key, by = accept-list \\| remembered, decision_id } }` (CART-1179). The LEDGER: one git note per commit on `refs/notes/cartograph` — `nvim --headless -u NONE -l tools/provledger.lua write [<rev>]` / `show [<rev>]`; `.githooks/post-commit` writes it after every commit (never fails a commit). In Lua: `require('cartograph.provenance').attribute(repo, range)` (the shared line-level attribution), `.ledger_row`, `.write_note`, `.read_note`. Notes travel only when pushed (`git push origin refs/notes/cartograph`). ★ The ledger only TIGHTENS: a note claiming a decision accepted answers nothing (pinned). An entry explains ONLY the commit its change landed in (CART-1195): made no later than the commit, not already in its parent, and — when older than the parent commit — none of it in the parent; before, 22 of 135 entries were credited to several commits. CART-1180 |\n| May this record LEAVE THE MACHINE? (a ledger note, a token, an invocation — does it carry an untracked file's bytes, a `.env`?) | `require('cartograph.sensitive')` — `classify(root, rels)` → `{ [rel] = why }`: DERIVED, a file git tracks is public, untracked/ignored is sensitive, a world with no repo is all sensitive; user `config.at(<abs>, 'sensitive') = true/false` overrides (never the tree). `reference(v)` = what travels in a sensitive value's place (`{ ref = 'sha256:…', sensitive = true }`). `leaks(record, images)` = the EGRESS check, independent of the redaction: any line (≥ 12 chars) of a sensitive file's images anywhere in the record's strings → `{ file, why }`, the bytes never named. Wired: every journal entry now records its INVOCATION (`{ verb, args, where }`, CART-1191 leaf 1 — local); the ledger note carries each entry's invocation with paths named `@<world id>/…`, or — when the entry touched a sensiti