r stdlib; `defines` a vantage that picks one -ifdef variant, none = the set over builds); `erlterms.apply(fun_term, args, S)` applies a closure; `erlterms.match(pat, subj)` is the three-valued clause test |\n| Which recursions in a tree are closed forms and which need a fixpoint — each carried argument invariant / decreasing / accumulating / rebuilt / other (and why a loop iterates at run time) | `tools/carriedcensus.lua [ONLY=<population>]` (syntactic); at run time `erlterms.carried` + the recursive-entry line of `tools/xmppserver.lua --sends` (CART-1136) |\n| Derive a generator from the code that INTERPRETS the sites (erlang: a `lists:foreach` fun of tagged-tuple clauses; heads = forms, guards = three-valued discriminators, bodies = effects, the caller chain = context and population) | `require('cartograph.erlderive').find(src, file)` → interpreters; `.context_chain(it, files)`; `.generator(it, chain, spec)` → a declaration for `generators.read`. ejabberd: add_registrations derived, erlreg 26/26 independently, plus 225 hook and 6 command facts |\n| Carry an edit made to ONE near-clone to the rest of its family (linked editing), through the journal | MCP `txn_plan_propagate { node|ref, text, scope? }` — or `require('cartograph.propagate').plan(store, { node, text, scope })`, or the tactic verb `propagate` (compose.VERBS, re-run is empty). The edit is classified by `clones.family_propagate` (value / template / mixed; straddle and unsupported refuse `unbuilt`); the ALGEBRA's commit decides who takes what (`scope` = member | class | all | clean). Without a scope the plan is the origin only, with a `propagate-scope` DECISION hazard whose fixes name the wider scopes — a tactic stops there BEFORE writing. Each sibling is re-rendered from its OWN text (`clones.family_member_text`; a template change takes the edited text as donor only when an identity render proves the member's surface equals the origin's, and the member's own NAME is kept) and verified by reparse against 